Skip the XP orb merge event when nothing is listening.

ExperienceOrb#merge fired ExperienceOrbMergeEvent unconditionally, building two CraftEntity casts
and an event object per merge. The event can only veto the merge, so with no listener registered
the merge always proceeds - checking that first is exactly equivalent.

Orb merging runs continuously at any grinder, and more so with a configured XP merge radius, which
this project's tuned spigot.yml now sets.

--- a/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/entity/ExperienceOrb.java
+++ b/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/entity/ExperienceOrb.java
@@ -304,7 +304,12 @@
     private void merge(final ExperienceOrb orb) {
-        if (!new ExperienceOrbMergeEvent((ExperienceOrb) this.getBukkitEntity(), (ExperienceOrb) orb.getBukkitEntity()).callEvent()) {
+        if (ExperienceOrbMergeEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0
+            && !new ExperienceOrbMergeEvent((ExperienceOrb) this.getBukkitEntity(), (ExperienceOrb) orb.getBukkitEntity()).callEvent()) {
             return;
         }
